sudo -u postgres psql -c "\l"

# List tables in a specific db
sudo -u postgres psql -d jlpt_learning -c "\dt"

# Run a query
sudo -u postgres psql -d jlpt_learning -c "SELECT * FROM users LIMIT 5;"


Table	Purpose
User	Accounts — email, password (bcrypt), username, XP, streak
Vocabulary	Word list (N5–N1)
KanjiEntry	Kanji with on/kun readings
GrammarPattern	Grammar patterns with examples
FlashcardReview	SRS state per user per card (interval, nextReview, easeFactor)
UserProgress	Mastery % per level per skill
UserAchievement	Which badges a user has earned
LessonHistory	Lesson completions + XP gained
Auth system (JWT + bcrypt)
POST /auth/register — creates user, returns {user, token}
POST /auth/login — validates password, returns {user, token}
GET /auth/me — verifies token, returns current user from DB
/api/v1/dashboard and /api/v1/user/profile are now protected — returns real DB data for the logged-in user
Token is stored in localStorage under jlpt-auth and auto-sent on every request
Files created
server/prisma/schema.prisma — all models
server/.env — DATABASE_URL + JWT_SECRET
server/src/db.ts — Prisma singleton
server/src/lib/jwt.ts — sign/verify helpers
server/src/middleware/requireAuth.ts — auth guard middleware
server/src/routes/auth.ts — register/login/me routes
start-db.sh — start the DB cluster (run once per WSL session)
Every time you open WSL, run:

./start-db.sh          # starts PostgreSQL on port 5433
cd server && npm run dev   # starts API on port 4000